If this file exists in the current directory, then 'upgrade-massos' will access
its configuration file and trusted keys list ONLY from the current working
directory (e.g. git checkout source tree), and will disregard all locations on
the system where such files could be installed instead. This is designed for
the developers of MassOS to be able to easily test the software. It can also be
used in situations where you want to upgrade from a version of MassOS which IS
new enough to be supported by this utility, but is NOT new enough to have this
utility pre-installed.

The contents of this file (if any) have no impact on its functionality. You can
safely replace or delete this text if desired. However deleting the entire file
will prevent 'upgrade-massos' from running from the git source tree.
